  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday morning through next Monday)\nIssued at 159 PM EDT Tue Sep 15 2026\n\nTemperatures are expected to remain unseasonably high across much of \nGeorgia. Humid conditions are expected to bring heat index values \nback towards the triple digits as we approach the weekend. \n\nOvernight lows will also be on the rise with the return of the mid \n70s to much of the area. This doesn't do much in providing relief \nfrom the daytime heat; especially for vulnerable populations. Look \nafter each other, and keep an eye on pets and kids. Stay hydrated if \nyou plan to spend time outside.\n\nThunderstorm chances during the afternoon will be down to less than \n20% for much of the area through the week. The ridge is finally \nexpected to break down Sunday into Monday as a front approaches. \nIsolated thunderstorms will be possible on Sunday afternoon, \nbecoming more widespread on Monday but total rainfall is expected to \nbe less than an inch for much of the CWA through the forecast \nperiod.",
